)PANEL KEYLIST(ISRHELP,ISR)
)ATTR DEFAULT(%+_)
/*********************************************************************/
/* PANEL    : MBKFXH                                                 */
/* TITLE    : HELP - FX CURRENCY MAINTENANCE (FXMNT)                 */
/*-------------------------------------------------------------------*/
/* 2011-05-09 JNB  ORIGINAL                                          */
/* 2016-06-27 PDQ  TOLERANCE                                         */
/*********************************************************************/
  % TYPE(TEXT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE) SKIP(ON)
  + TYPE(TEXT) INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN) SKIP(ON)
  ] TYPE(TEXT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) SKIP(ON)
)BODY EXPAND(//) WIDTH(80)
%TUTORIAL -/-/- FX CURRENCY MAINTENANCE -/-/- TUTORIAL
%Command ===>_ZCMD                                                             +
+
+The FX rate table holds one record per currency: units of currency per
+one pound.  Group Treasury's fixing files (07:30 and 14:00) update the mid
+rates through FXRAT010.  This dialog maintains everything else.
+
]Actions+
+  %D+display  %A+add a currency (held, with an indicative mid rate)
+  %M+amend name / decimals / tolerance / max deal / SWIFT / card flags
+  %T+customer margin tiers   %S+status A (active) H (held) S (suspended)
+
]Status+
+  %A+quoted normally.  %H+quoted with a warning (FXSVC01) - set by
+   FXRAT010 when a fixing moves more than the tolerance.  %S+not quoted
+   at all (sanctions, currency withdrawn).  Activating needs a mid rate
+   dated today.
+
]Tolerance+
+   Maximum move between fixings, in percent, before the currency is held.
+   Default 5.00.  Volatile currencies (TRY, ARS) are set higher by
+   Treasury Risk; the limit here is 25.00.
+
]After you confirm+
+   The new record is written to MBK.PRD.FX.MAINT.<userid> and job FXMNT01
+   (IDCAMS REPRO REPLACE) is offered.  Nothing changes until it runs.
)PROC
  &ZUP = MBKMENUH
)END
